WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.371
A budget has a bad reputation.

2
00:00:03.451 --> 00:00:07.271
People picture tracking every
coffee and feeling guilty.

3
00:00:07.351 --> 00:00:09.732
Here's what a budget is really for.

4
00:00:11.032 --> 00:00:15.523
A budget is a plan for your money,
made before the month starts.

5
00:00:15.603 --> 00:00:20.086
You decide where your pay goes,
instead of wondering where it went.

6
00:00:20.166 --> 00:00:22.282
It's not about saying no.

7
00:00:22.362 --> 00:00:24.861
It's about saying yes on purpose.

8
00:00:26.161 --> 00:00:29.545
Most budgets sort money
into three buckets.

9
00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:34.802
Needs are the must-pays, like rent,
groceries and minimum debt payments.

10
00:00:34.882 --> 00:00:36.940
Wants are the fun stuff.

11
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.216
And future you is saving
and paying down debt.

12
00:00:40.296 --> 00:00:45.270
One common starting split
is 50, 30 and 20 percent.

13
00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:50.405
Say you take home $2,400 a month.

14
00:00:50.485 --> 00:01:00.535
With that split, $1,200 goes to needs,
$720 to wants, and $480 to future you.

15
00:01:00.615 --> 00:01:06.060
If rent is high, needs can take more for
a while, and the other buckets shrink.

16
00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.751
Here's the part most people miss.

17
00:01:09.831 --> 00:01:14.167
A plan you can keep beats a
perfect plan you quit in week two.

18
00:01:14.247 --> 00:01:20.242
Round the numbers, check in once a week,
and adjust next month if you overspend.

19
00:01:21.542 --> 00:01:22.960
Quick recap.

20
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.705
A budget is a plan you make
before the month starts.

21
00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:31.747
Most budgets use three buckets:
needs, wants and future you.

22
00:01:31.827 --> 00:01:35.512
And a plan you can keep beats
a perfect plan you quit.

23
00:01:36.812 --> 00:01:38.669
Time for a quick check.

24
00:01:38.749 --> 00:01:40.913
What is a budget mainly for?

25
00:01:40.993 --> 00:01:45.438
Answer three short questions below
the video to finish the lesson.

26
00:01:46.738 --> 00:01:47.817
Now try it.

27
00:01:47.897 --> 00:01:49.338
In your Money Map,

28
00:01:49.378 --> 00:01:53.884
write down your monthly take-home
pay and your three biggest costs.
